1
00:01:07,275 --> 00:01:08,818
<i>Lumos Maxima.</i>

2
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:10,903
EXTREME SPELLS

3
00:01:11,070 --> 00:01:12,947
<i>Lumos Maxima.</i>

4
00:01:14,907 --> 00:01:16,784
<i>Lumos Maxima!</i>

5
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:22,915
HARRY POTTER
AND THE PRISONER OF AZKABAN

6
00:01:46,230 --> 00:01:47,815
Harry! Harry!

7
00:01:47,982 --> 00:01:49,984
Harry! Open the door.

8
00:01:56,866 --> 00:01:59,202
Marge! How lovely to see...

9
00:01:59,368 --> 00:02:02,747
Uncle Vernon, I need
Please sign this form.

10
00:02:02,914 --> 00:02:04,248
WHAT is it?

11
00:02:04,415 --> 00:02:06,542
Nothing. School things.

12
00:02:06,709 --> 00:02:09,378
Later, maybe, if you behave.

13
00:02:09,545 --> 00:02:11,756
Only if she behaves well.

14
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:15,051
- So you're still here?
- Yes.

15
00:02:15,468 --> 00:02:18,095
What an ungrateful “yes”!

16
00:02:18,262 --> 00:02:20,223
My brother is doing you a great favor.

17
00:02:20,389 --> 00:02:24,727
I would have sent it
directly to an orphanage.

18
00:02:24,894 --> 00:02:29,273
Is it my Dudders, my dear little nephew?

19
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:31,234
Give us a kiss!

20
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:33,694
Take the suitcase upstairs!

21
00:02:33,861 --> 00:02:35,822
It's okay.

22
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:42,078
Finish that.
That's it, pretty Rippy.

23
00:02:43,079 --> 00:02:46,082
- Can I tempt you, Marge?
- A bit.

24
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:49,210
Excellent food, Petunia.

25
00:02:49,794 --> 00:02:51,796
A little more.

26
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:55,633
Normally I just chill something,
with the fact that I have 12 dogs.

27
00:02:55,883 --> 00:02:58,469
A little more. That is!

28
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:03,558
Do you want a drop of brandy?

29
00:03:03,724 --> 00:03:07,770
A little drop of brandy
for Rippy precious?

30
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:11,065
Why are you smiling like that?

31
00:03:11,232 --> 00:03:13,067
Where are you sending the boy?

32
00:03:13,276 --> 00:03:16,571
To San Brutus, a good institution
for lost cases.

33
00:03:16,737 --> 00:03:19,740
Do they use a rod in San Brutus?

34
00:03:23,202 --> 00:03:24,537
Yes, yes.

35
00:03:24,745 --> 00:03:27,415
I have been hit many times.

36
00:03:27,582 --> 00:03:30,167
Excellent.
I don't accept that...

37
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:33,504
...not to hit them
to those who deserve it.

38
00:03:33,671 --> 00:03:36,799
But don't feel bad
because of how this one came out, Vernon.

39
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:40,887
It's a matter of blood.
The bad blood comes out.

40
00:03:41,053 --> 00:03:43,222
What was the boy's father, Petunia, doing?

41
00:03:43,389 --> 00:03:46,392
Nothing. He didn't work.
I was unemployed.

42
00:03:46,559 --> 00:03:49,395
- And he was a drunk, no doubt?
- That's a lie.

43
00:03:49,562 --> 00:03:52,106
- What did you say?
- My dad was not a drunk!

44
00:03:55,109 --> 00:03:59,196
Don't worry, Petunia.
I hold things very tightly.

45
00:03:59,363 --> 00:04:01,198
I think you should go to sleep.

46
00:04:01,365 --> 00:04:04,619
Silence, Vernon.
You! Clean it up!

47
00:04:05,995 --> 00:04:08,998
The truth is, there is nothing
What to do with the dad...

48
00:04:09,206 --> 00:04:12,960
...but with the mother.
It is very common with dogs.

49
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:17,214
If the dog suffers from something,
The puppy suffers from the same thing.

50
00:04:17,381 --> 00:04:19,050
Shut up! Be quiet!

51
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:25,806
Sure!

52
00:04:25,973 --> 00:04:28,100
I'll tell you something...

53
00:04:49,538 --> 00:04:51,666
Vernon!

54
00:04:54,752 --> 00:04:56,504
Vernon! Do something!

55
00:05:39,964 --> 00:05:41,966
Stop!

56
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:47,096
I got you, Marge!

57
00:05:53,811 --> 00:05:55,604
- Don't you dare!
- Sorry.

58
00:05:56,814 --> 00:05:58,649
Oh, Vernon!

59
00:05:58,816 --> 00:06:00,568
Oh my god!

60
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:02,528
Marge!

61
00:06:04,238 --> 00:06:06,115
Come back!

62
00:06:09,577 --> 00:06:11,829
Please!

63
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:14,623
Marge!

64
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:18,878
Come back!

65
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,070
Bring her back!

66
00:06:44,236 --> 00:06:48,699
- Bring her and fix her!
- No! He deserves what happened to him!

67
00:06:49,158 --> 00:06:52,286
- Don't come near me.
- You can't do magic outside of school.

68
00:06:52,495 --> 00:06:55,498
- Yes? Test me.
- You can't go back now.

69
00:06:55,664 --> 00:06:56,999
You have nowhere to go.

70
00:06:57,166 --> 00:06:59,502
I don't care.
Anywhere will be better than here.

71
00:07:06,675 --> 00:07:09,804
Help! Help!

72
00:08:35,639 --> 00:08:37,474
«Welcome
to the Knight Bus...

73
00:08:37,641 --> 00:08:41,020
...emergency transportation
for the abandoned wizard.

74
00:08:41,187 --> 00:08:46,150
My name is Stan Shunpike.
and I will be your collector tonight.

75
00:08:49,904 --> 00:08:51,322
What are you doing down there?

76
00:08:52,072 --> 00:08:54,241
- I fell.
- So that?

77
00:08:54,491 --> 00:08:57,119
- It wasn't on purpose.
- Get on now.

78
00:08:57,328 --> 00:08:59,496
There is no need to wait for the grass to grow.

79
00:09:06,629 --> 00:09:09,673
- What are you looking at?
- Nothing.

80
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,592
Get on then!

81
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:14,595
I'll upload this. You come in.

82
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:34,406
Come on, keep moving.

83
00:09:49,171 --> 00:09:52,424
- Start, Ern.
- Yes, start, Ernie!

84
00:09:52,591 --> 00:09:54,843
There are going to be potholes!

85
00:10:05,562 --> 00:10:08,816
- What did you say your name was?
- I didn't say.

86
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:13,487
- Where are you going?
- To the Leaky Cauldron! It's in London.

87
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:16,615
Did you hear, Em? «To the Leaky Cauldron.
It's in London.

88
00:10:16,782 --> 00:10:19,118
If you order pea soup...

89
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:22,079
...eat it before it eats you.

90
00:10:25,499 --> 00:10:28,127
- But the muggles! Can't they see us?
- The muggles?

91
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:30,045
They don't see anything, right?

92
00:10:30,212 --> 00:10:32,756
No, but if you sting them, they feel it!

93
00:10:34,508 --> 00:10:37,594
An old lady in front!

94
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:48,856
Ten, nine, eight...

95
00:10:49,106 --> 00:10:52,443
...seven, six, five, four...

96
00:10:52,609 --> 00:10:54,236
...three, three and a half...

97
00:10:54,445 --> 00:10:56,238
...two, one and three quarters...

98
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:04,121
Who is that?

99
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:06,707
That man.

100
00:11:08,375 --> 00:11:10,169
Who is that?

101
00:11:10,377 --> 00:11:11,879
Who is...?

102
00:11:12,129 --> 00:11:14,465
That's Sirius Black, that's him.

103
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:18,302
Don't tell me you've never heard
talk about Sirius Black.

104
00:11:19,636 --> 00:11:21,889
He is a murderer.

105
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:24,683
And they locked him in Azkaban for being one.

106
00:11:25,351 --> 00:11:28,771
- How did he escape?
- Very good question, right?

107
00:11:28,937 --> 00:11:30,898
He is the first to achieve it!

108
00:11:31,857 --> 00:11:34,485
He was a great supporter of...

109
00:11:34,985 --> 00:11:36,487
...Who You Know.

110
00:11:37,196 --> 00:11:39,073
You have heard of him.

111
00:11:39,239 --> 00:11:40,824
Yes.

112
00:11:40,991 --> 00:11:42,326
I have heard of him.

113
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:47,664
Ernie, two buses ahead.

114
00:11:48,165 --> 00:11:49,833
They're getting closer, Ernie.

115
00:11:50,667 --> 00:11:52,878
We have them on us!

116
00:12:00,260 --> 00:12:02,679
Be careful with your head.

117
00:12:07,559 --> 00:12:09,520
Hey, friends? Friends?

118
00:12:09,728 --> 00:12:11,897
Why the long faces?

119
00:12:17,736 --> 00:12:20,197
Yes! We're almost there, almost there.

120
00:12:25,619 --> 00:12:28,997
- The Leaky Cauldron.
- Next stop, Knockturn Alley.

121
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:33,001
Ah, Mr. Potter, finally.

122
00:12:36,004 --> 00:12:38,715
- 'Start, Ern!
l
- Yes, start, Ernie!

123
00:13:01,905 --> 00:13:03,740
Room 11.

124
00:13:06,326 --> 00:13:07,661
Hedwig!

125
00:13:07,828 --> 00:13:10,664
You have a very clever bird, Mr. Potter.

126
00:13:10,831 --> 00:13:14,543
He arrived five minutes before you.

127
00:13:16,462 --> 00:13:21,091
As Minister of Magic, it is my duty
inform you that a few hours ago...

128
00:13:21,258 --> 00:13:24,928
...his uncle's sister was located
south of Sheffield...

129
00:13:25,095 --> 00:13:27,598
...circling around
of a chimney.

130
00:13:27,764 --> 00:13:31,518
We send to the Department in Charge
Undo Accidental Magic.

131
00:13:31,685 --> 00:13:36,482
They duly drilled it
and they modified his memory.

132
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:41,361
You will have no memory of the incident.

133
00:13:41,528 --> 00:13:44,114
So it's over...

134
00:13:44,281 --> 00:13:47,159
...and nothing happened.

135
00:13:47,826 --> 00:13:49,161
Pea soup?

136
00:13:49,328 --> 00:13:51,455
No, thanks.

137
00:13:51,622 --> 00:13:53,832
- Mr. Minister?
- Yeah?

138
00:13:53,999 --> 00:13:55,792
I don't understand.

139
00:13:55,959 --> 00:13:59,505
I broke the law. a minor
You can't do magic at home.

140
00:13:59,713 --> 00:14:02,716
The Ministry does not command
no one to Azkaban...

141
00:14:02,883 --> 00:14:05,427
...for inflating an aunt.

142
00:14:09,389 --> 00:14:13,936
On the other hand, running away like this,
given the state of things...

143
00:14:14,102 --> 00:14:16,563
...was extremely irresponsible.

144
00:14:16,813 --> 00:14:20,567
- "The state of things", sir?
- There is a murderer on the loose.

145
00:14:20,734 --> 00:14:22,569
Are you referring to Sirius Black?

146
00:14:22,736 --> 00:14:24,488
What does that have to do with me?

147
00:14:26,823 --> 00:14:31,620
Nothing, of course. You are safe!
And that's what matters.

148
00:14:31,828 --> 00:14:34,957
And tomorrow you will go to Hogwarts again.

149
00:14:35,123 --> 00:14:38,085
These are your new books.
I took the liberty...

150
00:14:38,252 --> 00:14:42,256
...to have them brought to you.
Now, Tom will take you to your room.

151
00:14:47,052 --> 00:14:48,387
Hedwig.

152
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:53,642
By the way, while you're here,
It would be nice if...

153
00:14:53,934 --> 00:14:56,395
...don't go anywhere.

154
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:20,294
The Monstrous Book
of MONSTERS

155
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:21,688
Cleaning service!

156
00:16:25,108 --> 00:16:27,361
I'll come back later.

157
00:16:34,951 --> 00:16:36,370
I'm warning you, Hermione!

158
00:16:36,536 --> 00:16:40,248
Don't let that beast come near Scabbers
or I will turn it into a pillow!

159
00:16:40,457 --> 00:16:42,501
It's a cat, Ronald!

160
00:16:42,668 --> 00:16:45,671
- It's his nature.
- Is that what they told you?

161
00:16:45,837 --> 00:16:48,382
- It looks like a pig with hair!
-And your rat...

162
00:16:48,548 --> 00:16:51,093
...it looks like a shoe brush!

163
00:16:51,259 --> 00:16:53,679
Don't worry, Crookshanks.
You ignore the bad child.

164
00:16:53,887 --> 00:16:55,472
Harry!

165
00:16:59,142 --> 00:17:02,229
- Egypt! How is?
- Fantastic!

166
00:17:02,479 --> 00:17:05,774
There are mummies, tombs,
Even Scabbers had fun.

167
00:17:05,982 --> 00:17:09,194
- The Egyptians revered cats.
- Yes, and also the beetles.

168
00:17:09,361 --> 00:17:12,489
- Are you showing the cutout?
- No, no one.

169
00:17:12,656 --> 00:17:14,908
No, if you don't count Tom...

170
00:17:15,075 --> 00:17:16,702
- ...a servant...
- ...the other...

171
00:17:16,868 --> 00:17:18,954
- ...the cook...
- ...the plumber...

172
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:20,831
- ...and the Belgian magician.
- Mrs. Weasley.

173
00:17:20,997 --> 00:17:22,874
How nice to see you, sweetheart.

174
00:17:23,041 --> 00:17:24,543
Do you have everything you need?

175
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:26,712
- All your books?
- Everything is up.

176
00:17:26,878 --> 00:17:28,296
All your clothes?

177
00:17:28,505 --> 00:17:29,881
Excellent.

178
00:17:30,048 --> 00:17:31,925
-Harry Potter.
- Mr. Weasley.

179
00:17:32,092 --> 00:17:35,595
- Harry, can I talk to you?
- Yes of course.

180
00:17:35,804 --> 00:17:38,432
- Hermione!
- Good morning, Mr. Weasley.

181
00:17:38,598 --> 00:17:42,227
- Are you looking forward to another school year?
- Yes, it's going to be wonderful.

182
00:17:45,313 --> 00:17:49,151
There are some people in the Ministry
who doesn't want...

183
00:17:49,317 --> 00:17:51,987
...to divulge what I'm going to tell you.

184
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:55,490
But I think you need to know the facts.

185
00:17:55,657 --> 00:17:58,243
You are in danger.

186
00:17:58,910 --> 00:18:01,371
In serious danger.

187
00:18:01,872 --> 00:18:04,541
Does it have anything to do
With Sirius Black, sir?

188
00:18:05,333 --> 00:18:07,711
What do you know about Sirius Black, Harry?

189
00:18:07,878 --> 00:18:11,590
- Only he escaped from Azkaban.
- Do you know why?

190
00:18:12,299 --> 00:18:15,093
13 years ago, when you arrested...

191
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:17,095
-Voldemort.
- Don't say his name!

192
00:18:17,262 --> 00:18:18,597
Sorry.

193
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:21,683
When you stopped You Know Who...

194
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:23,477
...Black lost everything.

195
00:18:23,643 --> 00:18:27,939
But to date,
remains a faithful servant.

196
00:18:28,106 --> 00:18:30,275
And in his mind...

197
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:33,445
...you're the only thing he's avoiding...

198
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:37,365
...let You Know Who return to power.

199
00:18:37,574 --> 00:18:39,701
And that's the reason...

200
00:18:39,868 --> 00:18:42,412
...for which he escaped from Azkaban.

201
00:18:42,746 --> 00:18:44,456
To find you.

202
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:47,584
And kill me.

203
00:18:48,502 --> 00:18:51,171
Swear to me that it doesn't matter what you hear...

204
00:18:51,338 --> 00:18:53,882
...you won't go after Black.

205
00:18:54,257 --> 00:18:55,592
Mr. Weasley...

206
00:18:55,759 --> 00:18:59,763
...why would I go after
from someone who wants to kill me?

207
00:19:02,474 --> 00:19:04,309
Ron!

208
00:19:05,018 --> 00:19:07,103
For the love of God!

209
00:19:07,312 --> 00:19:09,773
Don't miss it!

210
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:12,901
I didn't mean to inflate it.

211
00:19:13,109 --> 00:19:15,529
- I just lost control.
- Bright.

212
00:19:15,695 --> 00:19:19,282
It's not funny. He was lucky
that they would not expel him.

213
00:19:19,449 --> 00:19:21,201
I was lucky they didn't arrest me.

214
00:19:21,368 --> 00:19:23,411
Still, I think it's brilliant.

215
00:19:23,995 --> 00:19:26,331
Come in. The other cabins are full.

216
00:19:29,167 --> 00:19:30,544
Who do you think it is?

217
00:19:30,710 --> 00:19:33,588
- It's Professor R.J. Lupin.
- Do you know everything?

218
00:19:33,755 --> 00:19:35,882
How does he know everything?

219
00:19:36,049 --> 00:19:39,177
It's in your suitcase, Ronald.

220
00:19:39,469 --> 00:19:42,764
- Do you think he's really asleep?
- It seems so. Because?

221
00:19:44,474 --> 00:19:46,643
I need to tell you something.

222
00:19:59,823 --> 00:20:03,159
Let me see if I understood.
Did Sirius Black escape...

223
00:20:03,326 --> 00:20:05,161
- ...to chase you?
- Yes.

224
00:20:05,328 --> 00:20:07,330
But they're going to catch him, right?

225
00:20:07,497 --> 00:20:10,208
- Everyone is looking for him.
- Clear.

226
00:20:10,375 --> 00:20:13,712
But no one had escaped
before Azkaban...

227
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:17,883
- ...and he's a murderous lunatic.
- Thanks, Ron.

228
00:20:19,342 --> 00:20:20,969
Why do we stop?

229
00:20:22,012 --> 00:20:23,763
We're not there yet.

230
00:20:28,018 --> 00:20:30,228
What's up?

231
00:20:30,437 --> 00:20:33,106
I don't know. Maybe the train broke down.

232
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:37,360
Oh, you stepped on me!

233
00:20:38,236 --> 00:20:40,196
Something is moving outside.

234
00:20:53,752 --> 00:20:56,796
I think someone is going to board!

235
00:21:21,988 --> 00:21:24,866
Damn! What is happening?

236
00:22:30,807 --> 00:22:32,892
Harry!

237
00:22:37,147 --> 00:22:38,565
Harry!

238
00:22:39,649 --> 00:22:41,484
Harry, are you okay?

239
00:22:47,657 --> 00:22:49,325
Thank you.

240
00:22:50,493 --> 00:22:52,954
Eat that. It will help you.

241
00:22:53,455 --> 00:22:55,582
Don't worry, it's chocolate.

242
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:03,965
What was that thing that came?

243
00:23:04,132 --> 00:23:07,552
It was a dementor.
An Azkaban guard. It's already gone.

244
00:23:07,719 --> 00:23:10,430
I was looking
to Sirius Black on the train.

245
00:23:10,597 --> 00:23:14,225
With your permission,
I need to talk to the driver.

246
00:23:18,855 --> 00:23:21,733
Eat. You will feel better.

247
00:23:27,530 --> 00:23:28,865
What happened to me?

248
00:23:29,032 --> 00:23:30,784
You stiffened.

249
00:23:30,950 --> 00:23:34,120
We thought that maybe
I had given you an attack.

250
00:23:35,872 --> 00:23:37,665
And either of you two...

251
00:23:37,874 --> 00:23:39,167
...you know...

252
00:23:39,375 --> 00:23:42,420
- ...did he faint?
- No.

253
00:23:42,587 --> 00:23:44,297
But I felt strange.

254
00:23:44,464 --> 00:23:46,299
As if they took away my joy.

255
00:23:47,550 --> 00:23:49,761
But someone was screaming.

256
00:23:49,928 --> 00:23:51,304
A woman.

257
00:23:52,263 --> 00:23:54,265
