at night on the train...

505
00:46:01,466 --> 00:46:04,010
- ...and the dementor.
- I'm very impressed.

506
00:46:04,219 --> 00:46:07,055
So what you fear most
It is fear itself.

507
00:46:07,222 --> 00:46:08,723
Which is very wise.

508
00:46:08,890 --> 00:46:10,976
Before I faint...

509
00:46:11,226 --> 00:46:13,228
...I heard something.

510
00:46:13,770 --> 00:46:15,397
To a woman...

511
00:46:15,856 --> 00:46:17,232
...screaming.

512
00:46:17,399 --> 00:46:20,652
Dementors bring us back to life
our worst memories.

513
00:46:20,861 --> 00:46:23,780
Our pain becomes his power.

514
00:46:24,614 --> 00:46:26,825
I think it was my mom...

515
00:46:26,992 --> 00:46:29,244
...the night she was murdered.

516
00:46:30,829 --> 00:46:35,292
The first time I saw you, Harry,
I recognized you immediately.

517
00:46:35,876 --> 00:46:38,753
Not because of your scar, but because of your eyes.

518
00:46:39,129 --> 00:46:41,298
They're your mom's, Lily's.

519
00:46:42,257 --> 00:46:43,675
Yes.

520
00:46:44,009 --> 00:46:47,012
Oh yes, I knew her.

521
00:46:49,347 --> 00:46:53,185
Your mother supported me and helped me
when no one else wanted to.

522
00:46:53,393 --> 00:46:56,605
Not only was she a very talented witch...

523
00:46:56,771 --> 00:47:00,108
...she was also a woman
extremely friendly.

524
00:47:00,609 --> 00:47:03,695
I had a way of seeing
the beauty in others.

525
00:47:03,862 --> 00:47:06,615
Even, and perhaps what is most special...

526
00:47:06,781 --> 00:47:10,035
...when the person couldn't see
beauty itself.

527
00:47:11,495 --> 00:47:14,206
And your father, James, on the other hand...

528
00:47:16,416 --> 00:47:19,794
...he had a certain talent
to get into trouble.

529
00:47:22,047 --> 00:47:27,552
A talent, say evil tongues,
that you inherited.

530
00:47:31,556 --> 00:47:34,518
You are more similar to them than you think.

531
00:47:35,352 --> 00:47:38,480
Over time you will come to see how much.

532
00:47:42,150 --> 00:47:46,321
Honeydukes is sensational. But nothing
like Zonko's joke shop.

533
00:47:46,530 --> 00:47:49,074
We couldn't go
to the Shrieking House. It's...

534
00:47:49,241 --> 00:47:53,328
The building with the most ghosts
From Britain, I know.

535
00:47:54,663 --> 00:47:56,164
What's up?

536
00:47:56,331 --> 00:47:58,792
Maybe Neville came back
to forget the password.

537
00:47:58,959 --> 00:48:01,378
You are there.

538
00:48:01,545 --> 00:48:05,840
Let me pass, please.
With permission! I'm a Delegate!

539
