744
01:06:02,791 --> 01:06:05,085
Ron, look!

745
01:06:10,799 --> 01:06:13,427
- Sorry! With permission!
- Merry christmas.

746
01:06:51,840 --> 01:06:53,676
Harry, what happened?

747
01:06:56,178 --> 01:06:58,305
He was his friend...

748
01:06:58,806 --> 01:07:01,058
...and betrayed them.

749
01:07:01,850 --> 01:07:03,811
He was his friend!

750
01:07:06,063 --> 01:07:08,023
I hope you find me.

751
01:07:08,649 --> 01:07:10,984
Because when you find me,
I'll be ready.

752
01:07:11,485 --> 01:07:14,071
When he finds me, I will kill him!

753
01:07:28,335 --> 01:07:30,003
<i>Harry?</i>

754
01:07:30,504 --> 01:07:32,131
<i>There you are. You came.</i>

755
01:07:32,506 --> 01:07:36,385
Are you sure you want to learn?
It is very advanced magic.

756
01:07:36,552 --> 01:07:39,012
Much further
of the ordinary level of magic.

757
01:07:39,179 --> 01:07:40,723
I'm sure.

758
01:07:41,306 --> 01:07:43,767
Well, everything is ready.

759
01:07:44,017 --> 01:07:47,396
I'll try to teach you
the "Patronus Charm."

760
01:07:47,604 --> 01:07:49,064
Have you heard of him?

761
01:07:49,231 --> 01:07:50,899
No?

762
01:07:51,066 --> 01:07:54,653
A patronus is a positive force.
For the one who conjures it...

763
01:07:54,820 --> 01:07:57,948
...acts as a shield,
with the dementor feeding on him...

764
01:07:58,115 --> 01:07:59,491
...and not from the magician.

765
01:07:59,658 --> 01:08:03,495
But for it to work,
you need to think of a memory.

766
01:08:03,662 --> 01:08:07,624
In a very happy memory,
a very powerful memory.

767
01:08:07,833 --> 01:08:11,628
Can you do it?
Yeah? Very good.

768
01:08:12,838 --> 01:08:15,048
Close your eyes.

769
01:08:16,842 --> 01:08:18,719
Focus.

770
01:08:19,970 --> 01:08:22,055
Explore your past.

771
01:08:22,556 --> 01:08:24,433
Do you have a memory?

772
01:08:26,059 --> 01:08:28,228
Let it fill you.

773
01:08:28,937 --> 01:08:31,064
Get lost inside it.

774
01:08:31,356 --> 01:08:36,695
And then say the<i>incantation,
Expecto Patronum.</i>

775
01:08:38,989 --> 01:08:39,990
Very good.

776
01:08:43,744 --> 01:08:47,080
Shall we start? Wand ready.

777
01:09:04,598 --> 01:09:07,518
<i>Expecto Patronum!</i>

778
01:09:07,976 --> 01:09:11,647
<i>Expectom!</i>

779
01:09:15,609 --> 01:09:19,696
That's it. Come on. Sit down.
Take a deep breath.

780
01:09:19,988 --> 01:09:23,784
It's okay. I didn't expect
that you did it the first time.

781
01:09:24,201 --> 01:09:29,331
It would have been extraordinary.
Eat this. You will feel better.

782
01:09:30,165 --> 01:09:33,043
- What a horrible dementor.
- No.

783
01:09:33,252 --> 01:09:36,004
That was a boggart, Harry.
A boggart.

784
01:09:36,171 --> 01:09:39,341
A real one would be worse.
Much, much worse.

785
01:09:39,508 --> 01:09:42,135
Out of curiosity,
what were you thinking about?

786
01:09:42,302 --> 01:09:46,014
- What memory did you choose?
- The first time I flew on a broomstick.

787
01:09:47,224 --> 01:09:50,561
You need a much better one.

788
01:09:57,442 --> 01:10:02,698
There is another. He's not exactly happy.

789
01:10:04,658 --> 01:10:06,743
Well, yes it is.

790
01:10:06,910 --> 01:10:09,496
This is when I have felt happiest...

791
01:10:09,663 --> 01:10:13,667
- ...but it's a complicated matter.
- Is it strong?

792
01:10:18,005 --> 01:10:20,841
So let's try.
Do you feel ready?

793
01:10:22,676 --> 01:10:24,386
Just do it.

794
01:10:34,438 --> 01:10:37,691
<i>Expecto Patronum!</i>

795
01:11:07,554 --> 01:11:10,974
Well done, Harry! Very good!

796
01:11:11,516 --> 01:11:15,646
- I think that's enough for today.
- Yes. Sit down.

797
01:11:15,812 --> 01:11:18,231
Eat this, it always helps.
Really yes.

798
01:11:18,398 --> 01:11:20,192
And, just so you know...

799
01:11:20,359 --> 01:11:24,363
...I think you're as good as your father.

800
01:11:24,529 --> 01:11:26,573
Which is saying a lot.

801
01:11:28,742 --> 01:11:30,744
I was thinking about him...

802
01:11:30,911 --> 01:11:33,080
...and in my mom.

803
01:11:33,246 --> 01:11:35,499
Seeing their faces.

804
01:11:36,124 --> 01:11:38,835
They were talking to me.

805
01:11:39,002 --> 01:11:41,254
Nothing more talking.

806
01:11:41,421 --> 01:11:43,757
That's the memory I chose.

807
01:11:45,384 --> 01:11:47,844
I don't even know if it's real.

808
01:11:48,345 --> 01:11:50,514
But it's the best one I have.

809
01:11:59,773 --> 01:12:02,067
- What a beautiful day.
- Precious.

810
01:12:02,234 --> 01:12:04,236
Unless, of course,
that they have torn you to pieces!

811
01:12:04,403 --> 01:12:06,822
Broken to pieces?
What are you talking about?

812
01:12:06,989 --> 01:12:10,158
- Ronald lost his rat.
- I haven't lost anything!

813
01:12:10,325 --> 01:12:12,452
- Your cat killed her!
- Lie!

814
01:12:12,619 --> 01:12:15,956
You have seen how
his bloodthirsty beast...

815
01:12:16,123 --> 01:12:20,043
...always lurking.
And Scabbers disappeared.

816
01:12:20,210 --> 01:12:23,088
Maybe you should learn
take better care of your pets!

817
01:12:23,296 --> 01:12:25,340
- Your cat killed her!
- No!

818
01:12:25,507 --> 01:12:27,009
- Yes.
- No.

819
01:12:29,052 --> 01:12:31,680
How did the hearing go, Hagrid?

820
01:12:31,847 --> 01:12:35,142
First, the members of the commission...

821
01:12:35,308 --> 01:12:37,978
...they talked about why
we were gathered.

822
01:12:39,855 --> 01:12:41,565
And then I stood up and said my thing...

823
01:12:41,732 --> 01:12:45,652
...I said Buckbeak was
a good hippogriff, very clean.

824
01:12:45,861 --> 01:12:48,905
And then, Lucius Malfoy stood.
Well, you can imagine.

825
01:12:49,072 --> 01:12:52,284
Buckbeak said
It was a dangerous creature...

826
01:12:52,451 --> 01:12:55,495
...that could just as well kill you as looking at you.

827
01:12:55,704 --> 01:12:57,497
And then?

828
01:12:58,206 --> 01:13:00,917
And then, good Lucius asked for the worst.

829
01:13:01,084 --> 01:13:05,213
- They're not going to fire you!
- No, they didn't fire me.

830
01:13:07,340 --> 01:13:10,343
Buckbeak was sentenced to death!

831
01:13:37,204 --> 01:13:42,709
Spiders! There are... there are spiders!
Spiders. They want me to tap dance.

832
01:13:42,918 --> 01:13:45,462
- I don't want to dance!
- Tell them what you think.

833
01:13:45,670 --> 01:13:49,633
Yes. Tell them. I'm going to tell you.
I'll tell him tomorrow.

834
01:14:07,776 --> 01:14:09,945
<i>- Peter Pettigrew?
- A very ordinary boy...</i>

835
01:14:10,112 --> 01:14:13,240
<i>- ...who always followed Black.
- Black was ruthless.</i>

836
01:14:13,448 --> 01:14:15,909
<i>He not only killed Pettigrew, he destroyed him!</i>

837
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:27,462
- Turn off that light!
- Sorry.

838
01:15:10,714 --> 01:15:12,757
- Be careful, child!
- We're sleeping!

839
01:15:12,924 --> 01:15:14,259
Yes, that's right.

840
01:15:23,059 --> 01:15:25,645
Mischief done! <i>Nox!</i>

841
01:15:27,856 --> 01:15:29,191
Potter.

842
01:15:29,357 --> 01:15:32,819
Why are you walking
through the corridors at night?

843
01:15:32,986 --> 01:15:36,865
- I was sleepwalking.
- How you look like your father, Potter.

844
01:15:37,073 --> 01:15:41,828
He was also extremely arrogant.
He strutted around the castle.

845
01:15:42,037 --> 01:15:46,374
My dad didn't show off!
Neither do I.

846
01:15:47,125 --> 01:15:50,253
If you don't mind,
I would appreciate it if you would lower your wand.

847
01:15:53,757 --> 01:15:55,592
Empty your pockets.

848
01:15:57,260 --> 01:15:59,888
Empty your pockets.

849
01:16:02,807 --> 01:16:04,434
What is that?

850
01:16:04,601 --> 01:16:07,854
- A blank parchment.
- Oh, yes? Open it.

851
01:16:14,444 --> 01:16:18,031
Reveal your secrets.

852
01:16:21,910 --> 01:16:23,370
Read it.

853
01:16:25,830 --> 01:16:31,336
«Messrs. Moony, Wormtail,
Canute and Prongs...

854
01:16:31,544 --> 01:16:35,632
...greet cordially
to Professor Snape

855
01:16:35,924 --> 01:16:37,425
Continue.

856
01:16:38,593 --> 01:16:42,472
They ask him not to stick his long nose
in other people's affairs.

857
01:16:42,681 --> 01:16:45,225
- You insolent brat...!
- Teacher!

858
01:16:46,851 --> 01:16:49,562
Whoa, whoa, Lupin.

859
01:16:49,729 --> 01:16:54,442
Are you taking a walk in the moonlight?

860
01:16:55,819 --> 01:16:58,238
Harry, are you okay?

861
01:16:58,446 --> 01:17:00,907
That remains to be seen.

862
01:17:01,741 --> 01:17:05,495
I have confiscated an artifact
quite curious to Mr. Potter.

863
01:17:05,662 --> 01:17:09,207
Look at it, Lupin.
It's supposed to be your specialty.

864
01:17:09,374 --> 01:17:14,170
- It is clearly full of black magic.
- I seriously doubt it, Severus.

865
01:17:14,337 --> 01:17:17,841
It looks like a scroll
designed to insult...

866
01:17:18,008 --> 01:17:21,886
...to anyone who tries to read it.
It must be from Zonko's store.

867
01:17:22,095 --> 01:17:26,308
However, I will find out if he has
hidden features.

868
01:17:26,474 --> 01:17:29,602
After all, as you say,
It's my specialty.

869
01:17:29,769 --> 01:17:33,106
Harry, come with me please.
Professor, good evening.

870
01:17:33,356 --> 01:17:34,649
Come here.

871
01:17:39,112 --> 01:17:41,865
Are you deaf? Turn off that light!

872
01:17:46,953 --> 01:17:48,413
Come in!

873
01:17:50,206 --> 01:17:55,420
I have no idea how it got there
this map at your power.

874
01:17:55,628 --> 01:18:00,091
Frankly, it amazes me.
that you have not given it to us.

875
01:18:00,258 --> 01:18:03,928
Didn't it occur to you that this,
in the hands of Sirius Black...

876
01:18:04,137 --> 01:18:06,139
...is it a map to find you?

877
01:18:06,931 --> 01:18:09,392
- No.
- No, sir.

878
01:18:11,394 --> 01:18:14,439
Your father never cared
Not much rules either.

879
01:18:14,647 --> 01:18:18,943
But he and your mother gave their lives
to save yours.

880
01:18:19,569 --> 01:18:23,656
Put your sacrifice on the line
walking through the castle alone...

881
01:18:23,823 --> 01:18:28,286
...with a murderer on the loose it is
a bad way to pay it back!

882
01:18:28,495 --> 01:18:30,663
I won't lie for you again.

883
01:18:30,830 --> 01:18:33,291
- Do you understand me?
- Yes sir.

884
01:18:33,458 --> 01:18:37,128
I want you to go back to your bedroom
and you stay there.

885
01:18:37,295 --> 01:18:42,050
And no deviating.
If you stray, I'll know.

886
01:18:46,721 --> 01:18:51,184
Professor, I don't believe that map
always works well.

887
01:18:52,018 --> 01:18:56,981
A while ago he showed me someone in the castle
I know he's dead.

888
01:18:57,399 --> 01:19:00,151
Oh yeah?
And who did he show you?

889
01:19:00,318 --> 01:19:01,861
To Peter Pettigrew.

890
01:19:04,489 --> 01:19:06,574
It's not possible.

891
01:19:07,784 --> 01:19:09,452
It's just what I saw.

892
01:19:12,288 --> 01:19:13,998
Good evening, professor.

893
01:19:17,502 --> 01:19:21,673
Expand your minds!
They must look further!

894
01:19:21,840 --> 01:19:27,262
The art of crystal ball gazing
lies in opening the inner eye.

895
01:19:27,429 --> 01:19:30,765
Only then will they be able to see.
Try again.

896
01:19:31,307 --> 01:19:33,393
What do we have here?

897
01:19:35,728 --> 01:19:37,939
Can I treat?

898
01:19:40,358 --> 01:19:43,319
Al Grim, possibly.

899
01:19:45,488 --> 01:19:49,576
Darling, from the first moment
when you set foot in my class...

900
01:19:49,742 --> 01:19:53,538
...I felt that you didn't have
the right spirit...

901
01:19:53,746 --> 01:19:57,625
...for the noble art of divination.
No. See, there?

902
01:19:57,792 --> 01:20:02,505
Your heart is so withered
like that of a spinster.

903
01:20:02,672 --> 01:20:05,717
Your soul, as dry as the pages
of the books...

904
01:20:05,884 --> 01:20:08,928
...to those who so desperately
you stick

905
01:20:24,444 --> 01:20:26,446
Did I offend her?

906
01:20:31,117 --> 01:20:33,119
Hermione has lost her cool.

907
01:20:33,286 --> 01:20:36,122
It's not that I haven't been
always crazy...

908
01:20:36,289 --> 01:20:38,875
...but now anyone
can realize.

909
01:20:39,042 --> 01:20:41,211
Wait.

910
01:20:41,419 --> 01:20:44,297
- We have to return this.
- I'm not going back.

911
01:20:44,631 --> 01:20:48,051
- Well, see you later.
- See you.

912
01:21:25,838 --> 01:21:31,094
<i>Harry Potter...</i>

913
01:21:37,976 --> 01:21:42,230
- Professor Trelawney...
-He will return tonight.

914
01:21:42,397 --> 01:21:44,023
Excuse me?

915
01:21:44,232 --> 01:21:48,861
Tonight, the one who betrayed
to his friends, whose heart is rotten...

916
01:21:49,028 --> 01:21:51,072
...will be released.

917
01:21:51,239 --> 01:21:53,491
Innocent blood will be shed...

918
01:21:53,658 --> 01:21:59,664
...and servant and master
They will come together once again.

919
01:22:06,004 --> 01:22:09,257
Sorry, dear. Did you say something?

920
01:22:10,049 --> 01:22:11,884
Nope!

921
01:22:12,302 --> 01:22:13,886
Nothing!

922
01:23:06,439 --> 01:23:10,485
I can't believe they're going
to kill Buckbeak.

923
01:23:10,652 --> 01:23:13,404
- And things get worse!
- Dad said...

924
01:23:13,571 --> 01:23:17,742
...that I could keep the head.
I think I'm going to donate it to the common room.

925
01:23:19,911 --> 01:23:22,747
- Look who came.
- Are you coming to see the show?

926
01:23:22,955 --> 01:23:26,042
Vile, hateful, perverse cockroach!

927
01:23:26,209 --> 01:23:27,960
Hermione, no!

928
01:23:28,544 --> 01:23:30,797
It's not worth it.

929
01:23:44,894 --> 01:23:46,979
Malfoy, are you okay?

930
01:23:47,146 --> 01:23:48,981
Let's go!

931
01:23:51,526 --> 01:23:55,988
- That made me happy.
- It was fantastic!

932
01:24:15,383 --> 01:24:19,679
Look at it. Love the smell of trees
when the wind blows.

933
01:24:19,846 --> 01:24:22,140
Why don't we set him free?

934
01:24:22,306 --> 01:24:25,977
They would know it was me and we would put
Dumbledore in trouble.

935
01:24:26,144 --> 01:24:27,895
He's coming, Dumbledore.

936
01:24:28,062 --> 01:24:30,440
He wants to be with me when...

937
01:24:31,441 --> 01:24:33,484
When it happens.

938
01:24:33,651 --> 01:24:35,027
He is a great man, Dumbledore.

939
01:24:36,028 --> 01:24:37,530
A great man.

940
01:24:40,032 --> 01:24:42,994
- We'll stay too.
- No way!

941
01:24:43,161 --> 01:24:46,330
Do you think I want you to see
such a thing? No!

942
01:24:46,539 --> 01:24:50,168
Have your tea and go.
Before you go, Ron...

943
01:24:57,592 --> 01:24:59,969
Scabbers! You are alive!

944
01:25:00,136 --> 01:25:03,848
- Keep a better eye on your pets.
- You owe someone an apology.

945
01:25:04,056 --> 01:25:07,769
The next time I see Crookshanks,
I will ask for forgiveness.

946
01:25:07,935 --> 01:25:09,061
I meant me!

947
01:25:09,729 --> 01:25:11,939
Heavens! What was that?

948
01:25:18,404 --> 01:25:19,822
Hagrid!

949
01:25:21,741 --> 01:25:23,075
Wow!

950
01:25:27,497 --> 01:25:31,584
It's late. It's almost dark now.
They shouldn't be here.

951
01:25:31,751 --> 01:25:35,546
If anyone sees them outside at this time,
It's going to be bad for them!

952
01:25:35,713 --> 01:25:39,300
And especially to you, Harry!
I'll be with you in a moment!

953
01:25:40,718 --> 01:25:43,137
Soon! Soon!

954
01:25:43,304 --> 01:25:45,056
Hagrid!

955
01:25:45,223 --> 01:25:49,143
- Everything will be fine. Everything will be fine.
- Go, go!

956
01:25:50,978 --> 01:25:53,773
What you see, on that slope...

957
01:25:53,940 --> 01:25:58,444
- ...it's heather.
- Professor Dumbledore, Mr. Minister.

958
01:25:58,611 --> 01:26:03,533
Please come in and we'll have tea.

959
01:26:12,917 --> 01:26:16,504
The Commission's decision
for the Disposition...

960
01:26:16,671 --> 01:26:19,841
...of Dangerous Creatures
is that the hippogriff, Buckbeak...

961
01:26:20,007 --> 01:26:25,513
...which we will call "the condemned"
be executed this day, at sunset.

962
01:26:27,348 --> 01:26:29,225
Now, now, Hagrid.

963
01:26:33,980 --> 01:26:35,731
What?

964
01:26:35,898 --> 01:26:37,984
I thought I saw...

965
01:26:38,150 --> 01:26:40,278
- Forget it.
- Let's go!

966
01:27:46,594 --> 01:27:48,804
It bit me! Scabbers!

967
01:27:49,388 --> 01:27:50,973
Ron!

968
01:27:53,142 --> 01:27:55,853
Scabbers, come back!

969
01:27:57,355 --> 01:27:59,106
Wait!

970
01:28:05,029 --> 01:28:09,325
- Scabbers, you bit me!
- Do you realize what tree that is?

971
01:28:09,492 --> 01:28:11,786
That's not good. Ron, run!

972
01:28:14,914 --> 01:28:17,458
Harry, Hermione, run!

973
01:28:18,042 --> 01:28:19,669
It's the Grim!

974
01:28:26,676 --> 01:28:29,762
'Harry!
_-R _
n on! Ron, wait!

975
01:28:29,929 --> 01:28:31,931
Harry!

976
01:28:33,516 --> 01:28:34,809
Help me!

977
01:28:56,122 --> 01:28:58,124
Let's go!

978
01:29:00,042 --> 01:29:01,460
Move!

979
01:29:05,506 --> 01:29:07,299
Get down!

980
01:30:01,353 --> 01:30:04,315
- Sorry.
- Don't worry.

981
01:30:04,482 --> 01:30:08,402
- Where do you think this is going?
- I have a hunch.

982
01:30:08,944 --> 01:30:10,446
But I hope I'm wrong.

983
01:30:30,132 --> 01:30:33,302
We are in the Shrieking Shack.
It isn't true?

984
01:30:34,386 --> 01:30:36,013
Go up.

985
01:30:46,398 --> 01:30:47,775
Ron!

986
01:30:48,317 --> 01:30:50,945
'Ron! Are you OK!
- The dog! Where is?

987
01:30:51,153 --> 01:30:54,406
It's a trap!
He is the dog, an animagus!

988
01:31:08,254 --> 01:31:11,048
To kill Harry,
You'll have to kill us all!

989
01:31:11,215 --> 01:31:13,008
No. Only one will die today.

990
01:31:13,217 --> 01:31:15,136
Then it will be you!

991
01:31:21,350 --> 01:31:23,519
Are you going to kill me, Harry?

992
01:31:24,728 --> 01:31:26,564
<i>Expelliarmus!</i>

993
01:31:30,276 --> 01:31:34,446
Wow, Sirius.
We're pretty done, aren't we?

994
01:31:34,655 --> 01:31:37,700
Finally the flesh reflects
the inner madness.

995
01:31:38,284 --> 01:31:41,954
You are an expert on inner madness,
right, Remus?

996
01:31:52,339 --> 01:31:53,340
I found it!

997
01:31:53,507 --> 01:31:54,842
It's here!

998
01:31:55,009 --> 01:31:58,220
- Let's kill him!
- No! I trusted you!

999
01:31:58,637 --> 01:32:02,391
And all this time, he's been friends with him.

1000
01:32:03,100 --> 01:32:06,145
It's a werewolf!
That's why he missed classes.

1001
01:32:08,981 --> 01:32:10,649
How long have you known?

1002
01:32:11,150 --> 01:32:14,361
Since Professor Snape
He assigned us that task.

1003
01:32:14,570 --> 01:32:17,489
You are the brightest witch
of your age that I have known.

1004
01:32:17,656 --> 01:32:20,075
Stop talking, Remus!
We must kill him!

1005
01:32:20,284 --> 01:32:22,912
'Wait!
“I already waited!

1006
01:32:23,078 --> 01:32:25,497
For 12 years!

1007
01:32:26,123 --> 01:32:28,500
In Azkaban!

1008
01:32:38,010 --> 01:32:39,720
Very good. Kill him!

1009
01:32:40,304 --> 01:32:44,058
But wait a minute.
Harry has a right to know why.

1010
01:32:44,225 --> 01:32:45,809
I know why!

1011
01:32:46,018 --> 01:32:48,270
You betrayed my parents!

1012
01:32:48,437 --> 01:32:51,357
- Because of you, they are dead!
- No, it wasn't him.

1013
01:32:51,523 --> 01:32:53,442
Someone betrayed your parents...

1014
01:32:53,609 --> 01:32:57,112
...but it was someone who,
Until recently, I thought he was dead.

1015
01:32:57,321 --> 01:33:00,783
- Who was it, then?
-Peter Pettigrew!

1016
01:33:00,950 --> 01:33:04,078
And it's in this room, right now!

1017
01:33:04,578 --> 01:33:07,539
Get out, Peter!

1018
01:33:07,706 --> 01:33:10,709
<i>-Come out and play!
- Expe/liarmus!</i>

1019
01:33:13,671 --> 01:33:16,173
Revenge is sweet.

1020
01:33:16,340 --> 01:33:18,592
I really wanted to be the one to catch you.

1021
01:33:18,759 --> 01:33:20,052
Severus...

1022
01:33:20,219 --> 01:33:23,722
I told Dumbledore that you were
helping a friend enter the castle...

1023
01:33:23,889 --> 01:33:25,015
...and here is the proof.

1024
01:33:25,182 --> 01:33:26,517
Brilliant, Snape.

1025
01:33:26,684 --> 01:33:31,063
Again, you put your penetrating mind
to work and you drew the wrong conclusion.

1026
01:33:31,272 --> 01:33:33,941
With your permission,
Remus and I need...

1027
01:33:34,108 --> 01:33:39,113
- ...finish a matter.
- Give me a reason. I beg you.

1028
01:33:39,280 --> 01:33:42,241
- Severus, don't be stupid.
- You can't help it, it's already customary.

1029
01:33:42,408 --> 01:33:43,742
- Shut up.
- You shut up, Remus!

1030
01:33:43,909 --> 01:33:46,245
Listen to each other, fighting
like two old married men.

1031
01:33:46,412 --> 01:33:48,956
Why don't you go play
with your chemistry game?

1032
01:33:49,498 --> 01:33:52,001
You know I can kill you.

1033
01:33:52,459 --> 01:33:58,090
But why deny it to the dementors?
They really want to see you.

1034
01:33:58,257 --> 01:34:00,968
Do I detect a flash of fear? Oh yes.

1035
01:34:01,135 --> 01:34:04,638
The kiss of the dementor.
It's hard to imagine.

1036
01:34:04,805 --> 01:34:10,227
They say it's almost intolerable to see,
but I will make the effort.

1037
01:34:10,436 --> 01:34:12,688
Severus, please!

1038
01:34:13,731 --> 01:34:15,733
After you.

1039
01:34:20,154 --> 01:34:21,905
<i>Expelliarmus!</i>

1040
01:34:23,657 --> 01:34:27,244
-Harry! What did you do?
- You attacked a teacher!

1041
01:34:27,453 --> 01:34:30,205
- Tell me about Pettigrew!
- He was our schoolmate!

1042
01:34:30,372 --> 01:34:31,874
Our friend!

1043
01:34:32,041 --> 01:34:35,044
No. Pettigrew is dead.
You killed him!

1044
01:34:35,210 --> 01:34:38,422
That's what I thought until you mentioned
you saw it on the map!

1045
01:34:38,630 --> 01:34:41,425
- The map lied.
- The map never lies!

1046
01:34:41,633 --> 01:34:45,637
Pettigrew is alive! And it's there!

1047
01:34:46,055 --> 01:34:50,642
- Me? You're crazy!
- Not you! Your rat!

1048
01:34:50,934 --> 01:34:54,063
- Scabbers run in my family...
- Twelve years?

1049
01:34:54,229 --> 01:34:56,732
A long life for an ordinary rat!

1050
01:34:56,899 --> 01:34:59,193
- He's missing a finger, right?
- And?

1051
01:34:59,360 --> 01:35:01,362
The only thing they found
of Pettigrew was...

1052
01:35:01,528 --> 01:35:02,654
Your finger!

1053
01:35:02,821 --> 01:35:06,075
The coward cut it off
to pretend he died!

1054
01:35:06,241 --> 01:35:09,286
-And then he transformed into a rat!
- Teach me.

1055
01:35:11,872 --> 01:35:14,958
- Give it to him, Ron!
- What are you going to do to him?

1056
01:35:15,167 --> 01:35:16,210
Scabbers!

1057
01:35:16,377 --> 01:35:19,463
Leave him alone!
Let it go! What are you doing?

1058
01:35:41,944 --> 01:35:43,779
Remus?

1059
01:35:44,530 --> 01:35:46,031
Are you Sirius?

1060
01:35:46,198 --> 01:35:48,117
My old friends!

1061
01:35:53,747 --> 01:35:57,584
Harry! Look at you. You are identical to your father.

1062
01:35:57,751 --> 01:36:01,422
-To James. We were excellent friends...
-How dare you talk to Harry?

1063
01:36:02,256 --> 01:36:04,883
To talk about James in front of him?

1064
01:36:05,092 --> 01:36:10,305
- You betrayed James and Lily, didn't you?
- It wasn't on purpose!

1065
01:36:10,472 --> 01:36:13,308
The Dark Lord!
You don't know what weapons he has!

1066
01:36:13,517 --> 01:36:17,563
Ask yourself what you would have done!
What would you have done?

1067
01:36:17,729 --> 01:36:22,109
I would have died! I would have died
Instead of betraying my friends!

1068
01:36:24,278 --> 01:36:26,655
James wouldn't have wanted me killed!

1069
01:36:26,864 --> 01:36:32,536
Your dad would have forgiven me,
I would have had mercy!

1070
01:36:33,036 --> 01:36:37,249
You should have imagined that we
we were going to kill you. Together!

1071
01:36:37,416 --> 01:36:39,460
Nope!

1072
01:36:40,961 --> 01:36:44,923
-Harry, this man...
- I know what it is.

1073
01:36:45,090 --> 01:36:47,009
But we will take him to the castle.

1074
01:36:47,176 --> 01:36:52,264
- Bless you, child. Bless you!
- Get off!

1075
01:36:53,390 --> 01:36:55,767
I said we would take you to the castle.

1076
01:36:56,143 --> 01:36:58,353
Then let the dementors take over.

1077
01:37:02,274 --> 01:37:06,028
Sorry for the bite.
I guess it must be burning a little.

1078
01:37:06,195 --> 01:37:09,740
A little? A bit?
You almost took my leg off!

1079
01:37:09,907 --> 01:37:11,450
I wanted to catch the rat.

1080
01:37:11,617 --> 01:37:15,454
Normally, I have a disposition
very nice as a dog.

1081
01:37:15,621 --> 01:37:20,876
More than once, James suggested
to make the change permanent.

1082
01:37:21,043 --> 01:37:25,923
The queue doesn't bother me,
but fleas are terrible.

1083
01:37:38,477 --> 01:37:39,978
Good.

1084
01:37:44,983 --> 01:37:47,528
- You better go.
- No, don't worry.

1085
01:37:47,694 --> 01:37:49,112
Everything is fine. I will stay.

1086
01:37:49,863 --> 01:37:51,865
You go, I'll stay.

1087
01:37:52,157 --> 01:37:55,327
- Are you okay?
- Yes. Go away.

1088
01:37:56,870 --> 01:37:59,873
- That seems very painful.
- Very painful.

1089
01:38:00,040 --> 01:38:02,626
Maybe they'll cut it off.

1090
01:38:03,085 --> 01:38:05,754
Madam Pomfrey
He will fix it for you right away.

1091
01:38:05,921 --> 01:38:10,133
It's too late. It's ruined.
They will have to cut it off.

1092
01:38:11,385 --> 01:38:13,220
It's beautiful, isn't it?

1093
01:38:14,054 --> 01:38:17,849
I will never forget the first time
that I went through those doors.

1094
01:38:18,517 --> 01:38:21,687
I'd love to get back in
as a free man.

1095
01:38:23,855 --> 01:38:26,650
It was very noble what you did back there.

1096
01:38:27,442 --> 01:38:29,611
He doesn't deserve it.

1097
01:38:29,778 --> 01:38:32,948
My dad wouldn't have liked it
that your best friends...

1098
01:38:33,115 --> 01:38:34,658
...they became murderers.

1099
01:38:34,866 --> 01:38:38,537
Furthermore, if he dies, the truth dies with him.

1100
01:38:38,704 --> 01:38:41,081
If he is alive, you will be free.

1101
01:38:44,543 --> 01:38:47,879
Ron! Have I not been a good pet?
You won't let him give me up...

1102
01:38:48,046 --> 01:38:50,549
...to the dementors, right?

1103
01:38:50,716 --> 01:38:54,761
Pretty girl! Smart girl!
You won't let...

1104
01:38:57,222 --> 01:38:59,141
I don't know if you know, Harry...

1105
01:38:59,308 --> 01:39:03,395
...but when you were born,
James and Lily named me your godfather.

1106
01:39:03,562 --> 01:39:05,522
I already know.

1107
01:39:06,690 --> 01:39:10,736
I will understand if you want to stay
with your uncles...

1108
01:39:10,902 --> 01:39:13,405
...but if ever
you would like a different home...

1109
01:39:13,572 --> 01:39:16,074
Could I live with you?

1110
01:39:17,409 --> 01:39:20,537
It's just an idea,
But I'll understand if you don't want to.

1111
01:39:20,704 --> 01:39:22,456
Harry!

1112
01:39:37,721 --> 01:39:41,433
Remus, my old friend.
Did you take your potion today?

1113
01:39:42,726 --> 01:39:45,979
You know you are a great man!
This heart is what defines you!

1114
01:39:46,146 --> 01:39:48,065
This heart, here!

1115
01:39:49,441 --> 01:39:51,443
This meat is just meat!

1116
01:39:52,569 --> 01:39:54,655
<i>Expelliarmus!</i>

1117
01:40:04,748 --> 01:40:06,291
Harry!

1118
01:40:07,376 --> 01:40:10,337
Remus!

1119
01:40:16,551 --> 01:40:18,887
Run!

1120
01:40:28,897 --> 01:40:30,941
- Let's go.
- Wait!

1121
01:40:31,108 --> 01:40:36,196
Hermione! Bad idea, bad idea.

1122
01:40:36,363 --> 01:40:38,615
Professor?

1123
01:40:42,703 --> 01:40:44,246
Professor Lupine?

1124
01:40:52,003 --> 01:40:55,257
What a cute little dog. How nice!

1125
01:40:55,674 --> 01:40:58,218
There you are, Potter!

1126
01:41:32,043 --> 01:41:33,044
Sirius!

1127
01:41:33,879 --> 01:41:36,298
Come back, Potter!

1128
01:42:42,113 --> 01:42:43,532
Sirius!

1129
01:42:44,324 --> 01:42:47,285
Nope! Sirius!

1130
01:43:29,160 --> 01:43:32,038
<i>Expecto Patronum!</i>

1131
01:45:44,838 --> 01:45:47,215
Harry?

1132
01:45:48,133 --> 01:45:50,510
I saw my dad.

1133
01:45:50,719 --> 01:45:52,303
What?

1134
01:45:52,470 --> 01:45:54,014
He drove away the dementors.

1135
01:45:54,180 --> 01:45:55,598
I saw him on the other side of the lake.

1136
01:45:55,807 --> 01:45:57,434
They captured Sirius.

1137
01:45:57,642 --> 01:46:00,478
Soon the dementors will kiss him.

1138
01:46:00,645 --> 01:46:03,148
- Are they going to kill him?
- No, it's worse.

1139
01:46:03,356 --> 01:46:05,191
It's much worse.

1140
01:46:05,358 --> 01:46:07,736
They are going to suck your soul.

1141
01:46:09,446 --> 01:46:11,031
Director, you have to stop them!

1142
01:46:11,197 --> 01:46:14,367
- It's a mistake!
- It's true. Sirius is innocent!

1143
01:46:14,534 --> 01:46:16,745
- Scabbers is the culprit.
- Scabbers?

1144
01:46:16,911 --> 01:46:18,329
It's my rat, sir.

1145
01:46:18,705 --> 01:46:22,500
It's not really a rat. Well,
Yes it was, my brother Percy's rat.

1146
01:46:22,709 --> 01:46:26,379
- But now he has an owl.
- We know the truth.

1147
01:46:26,588 --> 01:46:29,090
- Believe us, please.
- Yes, I believe you, Miss Granger.

1148
01:46:29,340 --> 01:46:34,721
But the word of three 13-year-old wizards
will convince few.

1149
01:46:37,849 --> 01:46:40,602
The voice of a child, despite
of his honesty and truth...

1150
01:46:40,769 --> 01:46:44,522
...it means nothing to those who
They have forgotten how to listen.

1151
01:46:49,736 --> 01:46:52,280
It's a mysterious thing, time.

1152
01:46:53,448 --> 01:46:54,783
Powerful.

1153
01:46:54,949 --> 01:46:57,869
And when one interferes, dangerous.

1154
01:46:59,412 --> 01:47:03,041
Sirius Black is in the last cell
of the dark tower.

1155
01:47:03,875 --> 01:47:05,960
You know the laws, Miss Granger.

1156
01:47:06,127 --> 01:47:07,921
They are not to be seen.

1157
01:47:08,088 --> 01:47:11,758
And they would do well to return
before the last bell.

1158
01:47:11,925 --> 01:47:15,470
If not, the consequences
They would be unimaginable.

1159
01:47:16,012 --> 01:47:17,806
If they are successful...

1160
01:47:17,972 --> 01:47:20,809
...they will save more than one innocent life.

1161
01:47:22,644 --> 01:47:24,896
Three laps is enough, I think.

1162
01:47:29,734 --> 01:47:31,569
By the way.

1163
01:47:31,736 --> 01:47:37,575
When I have doubts, I have discovered
that it is wise to retrace my steps.

1164
01:47:37,742 --> 01:47:39,828
Good luck.

1165
01:47:40,328 --> 01:47:42,789
What the hell was that about?

1166
01:47:43,456 --> 01:47:45,792
I'm sorry, Ron,
but since you can't walk...

1167
01:48:14,779 --> 01:48:16,406
What happened?

1168
01:48:16,573 --> 01:48:18,867
- Where is Ron?
- 7:30.

1169
01:48:19,033 --> 01:48:20,910
Where were we at 7:30?

1170
01:48:21,077 --> 01:48:22,871
I don't know. On the way to Hagrid's house?

1171
01:48:23,037 --> 01:48:25,456
Come! And they can't see us!

1172
01:48:26,499 --> 01:48:28,334
Hermione!

1173
01:48:46,519 --> 01:48:49,189
Hermione! Hermione, wait!

1174
01:48:50,982 --> 01:48:54,569
- Please tell me what we are going to do!
- Are you coming to see the show?

1175
01:48:54,777 --> 01:48:57,614
Vile, hateful, perverse cockroach!

1176
01:48:57,780 --> 01:48:59,115
It's us.

1177
01:48:59,324 --> 01:49:02,243
Hermione, no! It's not worth it!

1178
01:49:02,493 --> 01:49:03,912
This is not normal.

1179
01:49:06,206 --> 01:49:08,583
This is a time turner.

1180
01:49:08,750 --> 01:49:10,960
McGonagall gave it to me
the first quarter.

1181
01:49:11,127 --> 01:49:14,505
This is how I have been arriving
to all my classes.

1182
01:49:14,672 --> 01:49:17,884
- Going back in time?
- Yes.

1183
01:49:18,051 --> 01:49:21,429
Dumbledore obviously wanted
that we return to this moment.

1184
01:49:23,723 --> 01:49:26,893
Something happened that he wants us to change.

1185
01:49:30,021 --> 01:49:31,356
What a good hit.

1186
01:49:31,522 --> 01:49:33,024
Thank you.

1187
01:49:34,025 --> 01:49:35,693
Malfoy is coming!

1188
01:49:36,611 --> 01:49:38,947
- Wait for me!
- Don't tell anyone!

1189
01:49:39,405 --> 01:49:42,492
I'm going to get revenge on that mudblood!
You'll see!

1190
01:49:42,659 --> 01:49:46,579
- That made me happy.
- It was fantastic!

1191
01:49:47,956 --> 01:49:50,541
Come on we need to go
to Hagrid's house.

1192
01:50:09,686 --> 01:50:12,230
Look! Buckbeak is still alive!

1193
01:50:13,690 --> 01:50:15,566
Of course!

1194
01:50:15,733 --> 01:50:17,735
Do you remember what Dumbledore said?

1195
01:50:17,902 --> 01:50:21,948
If we succeed, we will save
more than one innocent life.

1196
01:50:22,323 --> 01:50:23,658
Let's go!

1197
01:50:38,965 --> 01:50:40,967
A great man, Dumbledore!

1198
01:50:44,929 --> 01:50:47,056
Here they come. I better hurry.

1199
01:50:47,223 --> 01:50:49,726
Fudge must see Buckbeak
before stealing it from us.

1200
01:50:49,892 --> 01:50:52,353
If not, he'll think Hagrid freed him.

1201
01:50:53,396 --> 01:50:55,773
Scabbers! You are alive!

1202
01:50:55,940 --> 01:50:58,735
- Keep a better eye on your pets.
- It's Pettigrew.

1203
01:50:58,943 --> 01:51:01,863
-Harry, you can't!
-He betrayed my parents!

1204
01:51:02,030 --> 01:51:05,033
- I won't just sit here!
- Yes, you have to stay!

1205
01:51:08,911 --> 01:51:11,622
Harry, you're in Hagrid's hut now.

1206
01:51:11,789 --> 01:51:14,625
If you enter, you will believe
that you went crazy!

1207
01:51:14,792 --> 01:51:17,670
Scary things happen to them
to those who alter time.

1208
01:51:17,837 --> 01:51:20,131
Don't let them see us.

1209
01:51:23,384 --> 01:51:25,136
Fudge is coming.

1210
01:51:26,012 --> 01:51:28,139
And we're not leaving.

1211
01:51:30,266 --> 01:51:31,851
Why aren't we leaving?

1212
01:51:42,779 --> 01:51:44,322
Are you crazy?

1213
01:51:50,328 --> 01:51:51,704
That hurt me!

1214
01:51:51,913 --> 01:51:53,247
Sorry.

1215
01:52:14,102 --> 01:52:16,771
We're leaving the back! Runs!

1216
01:52:34,205 --> 01:52:36,999
Is this what my hair looks like in the back?

1217
01:52:39,043 --> 01:52:40,378
What?

1218
01:52:41,254 --> 01:52:43,089
What I thought I saw...

1219
01:52:43,297 --> 01:52:45,967
- Forget it.
- Come on!

1220
01:53:00,273 --> 01:53:02,567
Go!

1221
01:53:08,823 --> 01:53:10,783
Stay away! Get off!

1222
01:53:11,659 --> 01:53:15,204
Mr. Minister,
You could use a cup of tea.

1223
01:53:15,371 --> 01:53:17,915
No, I don't want tea.

1224
01:53:22,587 --> 01:53:27,467
The executioner is acting
on behalf of the committee.

1225
01:53:28,593 --> 01:53:32,305
Well, gentlemen, shall we go outside?

1226
01:53:32,972 --> 01:53:36,392
Mr. Minister?
I think I should sign too.

1227
01:53:37,268 --> 01:53:40,396
Yes, perhaps it would be convenient.

1228
01:53:40,605 --> 01:53:44,400
Good. Buckbeak?
Soon, come with us.

1229
01:53:48,863 --> 01:53:51,574
Jala! Keep trying! Jala!

1230
01:53:53,951 --> 01:53:57,788
Is it okay? Soon, hurry up. Well.

1231
01:53:58,581 --> 01:54:01,876
-On the line, only your name.
- It's a very long name.

1232
01:54:02,293 --> 01:54:03,961
Hurry up, Buckbeak, okay?

1233
01:54:06,672 --> 01:54:09,634
Come on, Buckbeak!

1234
01:54:09,842 --> 01:54:12,136
Come get your dead little ferret!

1235
01:54:14,805 --> 01:54:19,310
- Come! Here it is! Come on, Beaky!
- That's it, Mr. Minister. Follow me.

1236
01:54:19,477 --> 01:54:21,145
Look there.

1237
01:54:21,354 --> 01:54:24,732
- Behind the rocks.
- What do you want me to see?

1238
01:54:24,899 --> 01:54:28,402
Professor Dippet planted
that heather when he was director.

1239
01:54:28,569 --> 01:54:31,405
- Yes, it's true.
- And all the strawberries.

1240
01:54:32,365 --> 01:54:35,243
- Come on, Buckbeak!
- I don't see strawberries.

1241
01:54:35,409 --> 01:54:36,577
There.

1242
01:54:38,704 --> 01:54:41,374
- Well, at the wrong step, hurry up.
- Well.

1243
01:54:43,042 --> 01:54:44,752
But where is it?

1244
01:54:45,670 --> 01:54:47,880
I just saw the beast!

1245
01:54:48,506 --> 01:54:50,716
- A moment ago!
- How extraordinary!

1246
01:54:50,883 --> 01:54:52,218
Buckbeak!

1247
01:54:52,426 --> 01:54:56,514
Come on, Dumbledore!
Someone dropped it!

1248
01:54:56,681 --> 01:54:58,933
-Hagrid?
- Professor, I swear I didn't do it!

1249
01:54:59,100 --> 01:55:02,478
The Minister is not implying
that you had nothing to do with it.

1250
01:55:02,687 --> 01:55:05,523
You were with us all the time.

1251
01:55:05,690 --> 01:55:07,567
I Exactly!

1252
01:55:07,733 --> 01:55:09,277
We must search the entire area!

1253
01:55:09,443 --> 01:55:12,488
Search the skies, if necessary,
Mr. Minister.

1254
01:55:12,655 --> 01:55:18,077
In the meantime I want a cup of tea
or a large brandy.

1255
01:55:18,244 --> 01:55:22,248
Executioner, we no longer require
of your services.

1256
01:55:22,415 --> 01:55:24,292
Thank you.

1257
01:55:24,500 --> 01:55:27,795
in this house
There are no small glasses, professor!

1258
01:55:38,556 --> 01:55:40,057
Over here! Come on!

1259
01:55:46,897 --> 01:55:48,649
Over here! Come on!

1260
01:55:51,068 --> 01:55:52,820
- And now?
- Sirius must be saved.

1261
01:55:53,029 --> 01:55:55,531
- How?
- I have no idea.

1262
01:56:04,832 --> 01:56:07,209
<i>- Look. It's Lupine!
<i>-lmmobulus!</i>

1263
01:56:13,633 --> 01:56:15,635
And here comes Snape.

1264
01:56:21,849 --> 01:56:23,517
And now we wait.

1265
01:56:24,727 --> 01:56:26,520
And now we wait.

1266
01:56:54,090 --> 01:56:57,343
At least someone is having a good time.

1267
01:57:00,137 --> 01:57:01,931
Hermione?

1268
01:57:02,098 --> 01:57:06,435
Before, by the lake,
when I was with Sirius...

1269
01:57:06,602 --> 01:57:08,729
...yes I saw someone.

1270
01:57:08,896 --> 01:57:12,316
That someone did
let the dementors go away.

1271
01:57:12,483 --> 01:57:13,818
With a patronus.

1272
01:57:13,984 --> 01:57:15,903
I heard when Snape
He told Dumbledore.

1273
01:57:16,070 --> 01:57:17,530
According to him...

1274
01:57:17,697 --> 01:57:21,117
...just a very powerful wizard
I could have conjured it.

1275
01:57:21,283 --> 01:57:23,160
It was my dad.

1276
01:57:24,286 --> 01:57:26,080
My dad conjured the patronus.

1277
01:57:26,247 --> 01:57:28,499
-Your dad is...
- Dead, I know.

1278
01:57:29,917 --> 01:57:32,253
I'm just telling you what I saw.

1279
01:57:36,382 --> 01:57:38,008
Here we come.

1280
01:57:43,681 --> 01:57:46,058
Do you see Sirius talking to me?

1281
01:57:46,225 --> 01:57:49,061
-He wants me to go live with him.
- Fantastic.

1282
01:57:49,228 --> 01:57:52,565
Since we will release it,
I will never return to the Dursleys.

1283
01:57:52,732 --> 01:57:54,358
I will live alone with him.

1284
01:57:55,025 --> 01:57:56,986
We can live in the country...

1285
01:57:57,153 --> 01:57:59,780
...in a place where you can see the sky.

1286
01:57:59,947 --> 01:58:02,783
You're going to like that,
after his years in Azkaban.

1287
01:58:03,826 --> 01:58:05,369
Harry!

1288
01:58:06,912 --> 01:58:08,622
Run! Run!

1289
01:58:15,546 --> 01:58:17,047
Let's go!

1290
01:58:36,609 --> 01:58:38,944
- What are you doing?
- Saving your life!

1291
01:58:43,199 --> 01:58:44,575
Thank you.

1292
01:58:46,410 --> 01:58:50,456
- Fantastic! He's coming here.
- I didn't think about that. Runs!

1293
02:00:05,573 --> 02:00:07,324
That was terrifying.

1294
02:00:07,491 --> 02:00:10,452
Professor Lupine
He's having a bad night.

1295
02:00:21,881 --> 02:00:25,009
Sirius! Come on!

1296
02:00:41,025 --> 02:00:43,152
- This is horrible.
- Don't worry.

1297
02:00:43,319 --> 02:00:46,530
My dad will come and conjure the patronus.

1298
02:00:55,247 --> 02:00:57,082
Any time!

1299
02:00:57,291 --> 02:00:59,335
Over there! You'll see!

1300
02:01:00,711 --> 02:01:03,213
Harry, listen to me. Nobody comes.

1301
02:01:03,380 --> 02:01:05,925
Don't worry! He is coming!

1302
02:01:10,763 --> 02:01:12,514
They are dying...

1303
02:01:14,558 --> 02:01:16,435
...both of them.

1304
02:01:18,520 --> 02:01:20,230
Harry!

1305
02:01:22,149 --> 02:01:26,028
<i>Expecto Patronum!</i>

1306
02:02:24,628 --> 02:02:26,213
You were right, Hermione!

1307
02:02:26,380 --> 02:02:29,717
I didn't see my dad before. I saw myself!

1308
02:02:29,883 --> 02:02:32,636
I saw myself conjuring the patronus before.

1309
02:02:32,803 --> 02:02:35,180
I knew I could do it
this time because...

1310
02:02:35,347 --> 02:02:37,057
...he had already done it.

1311
02:02:37,224 --> 02:02:39,685
- Does it make sense?
- No!

1312
02:02:39,852 --> 02:02:42,688
But I don't like flying!

1313
02:02:55,826 --> 02:02:57,161
<i>Bomber!</i>

1314
02:03:30,486 --> 02:03:33,280
I will stay with you forever
grateful for this.

1315
02:03:33,447 --> 02:03:34,782
To both.

1316
02:03:34,948 --> 02:03:37,868
- I want to go with you.
- Someday, maybe.

1317
02:03:38,035 --> 02:03:40,954
For a time,
My life will be very unpredictable.

1318
02:03:41,121 --> 02:03:42,873
And also...

1319
02:03:43,791 --> 02:03:47,086
- ...you must be here.
- But you are innocent.

1320
02:03:47,252 --> 02:03:49,379
And you know it.

1321
02:03:50,464 --> 02:03:52,382
And for now, that's enough for me.

1322
02:03:54,676 --> 02:03:57,221
You must be tired of hearing this...

1323
02:03:58,222 --> 02:04:00,766
...but you look a lot like your dad.

1324
02:04:02,518 --> 02:04:04,478
Except for the eyes.

1325
02:04:05,437 --> 02:04:07,731
- You have...
- My mom's eyes.

1326
02:04:09,691 --> 02:04:14,780
It's cruel that I could spend so much time
with James and Lily and you so little.

1327
02:04:15,405 --> 02:04:16,907
But you need to know this:

1328
02:04:17,991 --> 02:04:21,161
Those who love us never leave us.

1329
02:04:22,538 --> 02:04:24,498
And you can always find them...

1330
02:04:26,917 --> 02:04:28,752
...in here.

1331
02:04:39,138 --> 02:04:41,682
You really are the witch
brightest of your age.

1332
02:05:08,500 --> 02:05:10,127
We have to go!

1333
02:05:38,405 --> 02:05:41,074
- Well?
- He was free. We did it!

1334
02:05:41,241 --> 02:05:42,784
What did they achieve?

1335
02:05:42,993 --> 02:05:44,912
Good night.

1336
02:05:53,670 --> 02:05:55,005
How did they get there?

1337
02:05:55,172 --> 02:05:57,841
I was talking to you there,
and now they are there!

1338
02:05:58,175 --> 02:06:00,802
- What are you talking about, Harry?
- Don't know.

1339
02:06:01,011 --> 02:06:04,514
How can someone be
in two places at the same time?

1340
02:06:31,041 --> 02:06:32,542
Hello, Harry.

1341
02:06:36,129 --> 02:06:37,965
I saw you coming.

1342
02:06:42,552 --> 02:06:45,222
I've seen worse, believe me.

1343
02:06:47,933 --> 02:06:51,103
- They fired him.
- No.

1344
02:06:51,270 --> 02:06:54,231
The truth is, I resigned.

1345
02:06:54,398 --> 02:06:56,191
Did he resign? Because?

1346
02:06:56,358 --> 02:07:01,655
It seems that someone disclosed
the nature of my state.

1347
02:07:01,822 --> 02:07:07,327
At this time tomorrow, the Iechuzas
They will start to arrive and the parents will not want...

1348
02:07:07,494 --> 02:07:10,872
...than someone like me
give classes to your children.

1349
02:07:11,081 --> 02:07:13,000
-But Dumbledore...
Dumbledore...

1350
02:07:13,166 --> 02:07:15,043
...has already risked enough for me.

1351
02:07:15,210 --> 02:07:18,463
Besides, people like me are...

1352
02:07:19,089 --> 02:07:22,426
Well let's say that
I'm already used to it.

1353
02:07:31,977 --> 02:07:34,563
Why do you look so unhappy?

1354
02:07:34,730 --> 02:07:36,898
It was of no use.

1355
02:07:37,107 --> 02:07:40,610
- Pettigrew ran away.
- Was it of no use?

1356
02:07:40,777 --> 02:07:44,281
It served a lot.
You unearthed the truth.

1357
02:07:44,448 --> 02:07:46,950
You saved an innocent
of terrible luck.

1358
02:07:47,326 --> 02:07:49,828
Yes it helped a lot.

1359
02:07:54,458 --> 02:07:56,668
If I'm proud of something...

1360
02:07:56,835 --> 02:07:59,504
...is how much you learned this year.

1361
02:07:59,671 --> 02:08:02,424
Now, since I'm no longer your teacher...

1362
02:08:02,632 --> 02:08:06,845
...I don't feel guilty at all
to return this to you.

1363
02:08:07,763 --> 02:08:10,265
So now I say goodbye, Harry.

1364
02:08:10,432 --> 02:08:13,018
I'm sure we'll see each other again.

1365
02:08:13,560 --> 02:08:14,895
Until then...

1366
02:08:16,229 --> 02:08:17,939
...mischief performed.

1367
02:08:52,182 --> 02:08:56,395
Stand back, I said!
Or I'll take her upstairs, if you don't calm down.

1368
02:08:56,561 --> 02:08:57,979
Harry!

1369
02:08:58,814 --> 02:09:00,190
Where did you get it from?

1370
02:09:00,357 --> 02:09:02,776
Can I try it?
After you, of course.

1371
02:09:02,943 --> 02:09:05,112
- What are you talking about?
- Silence!

1372
02:09:05,278 --> 02:09:08,573
Let the man pass.
I didn't mean to open it.

1373
02:09:08,740 --> 02:09:11,243
It was badly wrapped. They forced me.

1374
02:09:11,410 --> 02:09:12,911
It's not true!

1375
02:09:14,287 --> 02:09:17,791
- It's a Firebolt.
- It's the fastest broom in the world!

1376
02:09:17,958 --> 02:09:19,501
For me?

1377
02:09:19,709 --> 02:09:22,212
- But who sent it?
- Nobody knows.

1378
02:09:22,379 --> 02:09:24,297
Came with this.

1379
02:09:30,971 --> 02:09:32,806
How fast is he, Harry?

1380
02:09:52,159 --> 02:09:53,785
Lumos.

1381
02:09:53,952 --> 02:09:56,371
<i>I solemnly swear that my intentions
They are not good.</i>

1382
02:09:59,833 --> 02:10:02,544
HARRY POTTER
AND THE PRISONER OF AZKABAN

1383
02:11:57,284 --> 02:12:00,996
HARRY POTTER
AND THE PRISONER OF AZKABAN

1384
02:21:15,550 --> 02:21:17,343
<i>Mischief performed.</i>

1385
02:21:19,512 --> 02:21:21,305
HARRY POTTER
AND THE PRISONER OF AZKABAN

1386
02:21:23,099 --> 02:21:24,559
<i>Nox.</i>
